<title>USA: Typhoon Violet threat to ships south of Japan-WSC.</title>
<headline>Typhoon Violet threat to ships south of Japan-WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, MASS. 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Typhoon Violet is a major threat to shipping south and east of Okinawa, Japan, private forecaster Weather Services Corp said.</p>
<p>Violet has top winds of 120 mph and is expected to slowly weaken during the next 36 hours, but will still remain a powerful storm as it tracks to the northeast, passing about 100-150 miles east of Okinawa.</p>
</text>
